WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.760
There are lots of good reasons
to try and follow a healthier diet—

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.880
you lose weight,
you feel good,

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.680
but the main reason?

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.200
To live a longer, happier,
more productive life.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.240
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.280
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.040
How can we improve the capacity of
our blood vessels to repair themselves?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.440
Here’s our first story.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.200
The capacity of our blood
vessels to repair themselves

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.320
is dependent on
endothelial progenitor cells

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.520
that emerge from stem cells
in our bone marrow

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.160
to patch up any holes
in our endothelium,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.280
the innermost lining
of our blood vessels

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.920
that keeps our blood
flowing smoothly.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.200
Lower levels of circulating
endothelial progenitor cells

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.760
in the blood correlates
with arterial diseases

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.720
like erectile dysfunction.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.040
Higher numbers,
on the other hand,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.320
are correlated with
a significantly reduced risk

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.360
of death
from cardiovascular causes.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.680
Before we explore
how to boost our levels,

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.440
let us first establish
cause-and-effect.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.440
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.880
was performed in men and women

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.280
with peripheral
vascular disease,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.240
a circulation disorder
characterized by the narrowing

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.720
of blood vessels outside
of the heart or brain.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.240
The arteries supplying
blood to their legs

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.120
were so ravaged by disease

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.240
that they could only
walk about a minute

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.680
before the muscles in their legs
cried out in pain

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.720
from lack of oxygen.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.920
For each study participant,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.480
one leg was randomly selected

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.160
to be injected with cells
from their own bone marrow

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.240
and the other was injected
with their own peripheral blood

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.080
as a control.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.480
Not only was pain-free walking
time significantly extended

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.040
in the marrow-injected leg,

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.600
they were less likely
to subsequently lose it.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.720
Severe limb ischemia,
lack of oxygen,

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.360
from peripheral
vascular disease

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.880
carries a 10 to 40 percent
amputation rate

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.480
within six months.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.000
In the control group,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.920
14 percent were forced
to undergo a major amputation

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.960
compared to zero
in the bone marrow group.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.640
Given these remarkable benefits,

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.360
the link between higher numbers
of endothelial progenitor cells

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.720
and lower risk of dying
from cardiovascular disease

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.440
may indeed by causal.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.280
Short of sticking a large bore
needle into your hip,

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.480
how else can we
cultivate and release

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.440
more endothelial progenitor
cells into our system?

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.840
Smoking cessation is one of the
most important and effective

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.120
lifestyle changes to increase
the number and function

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.240
of active endothelial
progenitor cells.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.720
Cutting down isn't enough.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.680
There are 20 cigarettes
in a pack.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.400
If you only smoke
about one a day,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.480
wouldn't you think you'd only
have one-twentieth the risk

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.760
of cardiovascular disease,

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.760
compared to smoking
the whole pack?

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.720
Based on a meta-analysis
of more than a hundred studies,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.120
smoking only about
one cigarette a day

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.920
caused around 10 times the risk
of cardiovascular disease

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.040
you'd expect by that logic,

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.400
compared to smoking
a pack a day.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.200
There is no
safe level of smoking

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.480
when it comes to heart attack
and stroke risk.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.680
Even exposure to second-hand
smoke can deteriorate

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.560
our circulating endothelial
progenitor cell count,

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.800
so even just being
around smokers is risky.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.120
Randomized controlled trials
show exercise training

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:26.000
can actually boost endothelial
progenitor cell circulation.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.880
In a study of middle-aged
and older sedentary men,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.040
for example, three months
of moderate aerobic exercise--

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.960
mostly walking,
with some participants

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.680
starting to jog a bit
as their fitness improved--

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.960
led to a doubling of
endothelial progenitor cells

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.640
in their bloodstream.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.280
Regular aerobic exercise
could be considered

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.200
a "first line" strategy

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.200
for helping to prevent and treat
arterial aging.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.520
What about diet?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.440
A randomized controlled trial
showed that reducing

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.400
saturated fat,
mostly in the form of butter,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.120
significantly elevated

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.400
endothelial progenitor
cell numbers,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.480
consistent with a study
on baboons showing that

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.640
even a few weeks
of a high-cholesterol,

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.880
high-fat diet
could cause dramatic

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.360
premature epithelial
cell senescence.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.160
Individual foods that
have been shown to increase

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.400
circulating endothelial
progenitor cells

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.120
include berries,
onions, and green tea,

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.760
and a diet centered completely
around whole plant foods

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.680
not only showed a boost
in endothelial progenitors,

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.120
but an improvement
in endothelial function,

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.760
along with a drop
in LDL cholesterol.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.720
In our next story,

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.760
we look at how vegetables
such as beets and arugula

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:43.200
can improve athletic performance by
improving oxygen delivery and utilization.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.200
It's great that we can improve athletic
performance eating a few beets,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.800
but so what if you run 5% faster?

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.160
It can be a fun experiment
to eat a can of beets

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.080
and maybe shave a
minute off your 5k time.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.040
But these are the people
who could really benefit

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.360
from a more efficient use of oxygen:
those suffering from emphysema.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.720
Yeah, young healthy adults
eating greens and beets

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:08.360
can swim, run, and cycle
faster and farther,

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.640
but what about those who get out
of breath just walking up the stairs?

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.400
Do nitrate-rich vegetables
work where it counts?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.320
Yes, significantly extended time

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.240
on the treadmill after
two shots of beet juice.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.920
It's great that beet
juice can decrease

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.040
blood pressures in
young healthy adults,

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:29.040
but what about in those who really
need it, older overweight subjects?

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.440
Just one shot of beet juice a day
versus berry juice as a control,

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.440
and in a few weeks a significant
drop in blood pressure.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.320
But within just a few
days after stopping

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.640
after three weeks
of beeting themselves up,

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.800
blood pressures went back up.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:48.760
So we have to eat our vegetables
and keep eating our vegetables.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.160
Why did it take until
2015 to publish a study

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.960
on lowering blood pressure in
people with high blood pressure?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.160
You'd think that'd be
the first group to try it on.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.240
Who's going to fund it,
though — Big Beet?

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:05.400
Blood pressure medications rake in
more than $10 billion dollars a year.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.760
You can't make billions on beets.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.760
But that's why we have charities
like the British Heart Foundation,

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.520
which funded a study to give
folks with high blood pressure

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.040
a cup of beet juice
a day for four weeks.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.360
After all, high blood pressure
may be the #1 risk factor

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.400
for premature death in the world.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:28.240
In ten years it could affect nearly
one in three adults on this planet.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.000
But put them on beet juice
and blood pressures dropped

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.640
and kept dropping until it
was stopped after a month.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.600
With so many people with high blood
pressure even despite treatment,

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.200
an additional strategy, based on the
intake of nitrate-rich vegetables,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.160
may prove to be both
cost-effective, affordable,

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:47.920
and favorable for a public health
approach to hypertension.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.600
What about those with
peripheral artery disease?

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:56.360
Tens of millions with atherosclerotic
clogs impairing blood flow to their legs,

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:59.880
which can cause a cramping pain
in the calves called claudication

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.200
due to lack of blood flow
through the blocked arteries,

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:06.080
severely limiting one's ability
to even just walk around,

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.908
but just drink some beet
juice and walk 18% longer.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.836
They measured the actual oxygenation
of their blood within their calf muscle.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.800
The nitric oxide from vegetable nitrates
not only improves oxygen efficiency

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:23.120
but oxygen delivery by
vasodilating blood vessels,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:26.080
opening up arteries so
there's more blood flow.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.320
I’m surprised beet
juice companies

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.720
aren’t trying to position
themselves as veggie Viagra.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.880
It could certainly explain why
those eating more veggies

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.840
have such improved
sexual function,

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.120
though this study was
a snapshot in time,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.360
so you can't tell which came first.
However, it seems more reasonable

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.840
that low fruit and vegetable consumption
contributes to erectile dysfunction,

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:50.000
rather than the other way around.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:55.200
What about the most
important organ, the brain?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:59.080
Poor cerebral perfusion – lack of
blood flow and oxygen in the brain –

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.400
is associated with cognitive
decline and dementia,

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.920
and they showed that
the nitrate in vegetables

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.360
may be beneficial in treating
age-related cognitive decline.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:10.080
They showed a direct
effect of dietary nitrate

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.680
on cerebral blood flow
within the frontal lobes,

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.880
the areas particularly
compromised by aging.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:20.400
This is a critical brain area for
so-called executive function,

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:24.560
basic task and problem solving,
important for day-to-day functioning.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.000
The nitrite from nitrate
has been shown

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.520
to not just increase blood
flow to certain areas of the body,

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:34.240
but also acts preferentially
in low oxygen conditions,

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.720
allowing it to increase blood flow

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.600
precisely in the areas where
it's needed the most.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.680
And that's what they
found in the brain:

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.760
increased blood flow to the
at-risk areas of the aging brain.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.080
And the only side effect
of beeting your brains out?

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.880
A little extra color in your life.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:57.480
Do legumes—beans, chickpeas,
split peas, and lentils—

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.800
work only to prevent disease,

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:03.760
or can they help treat
and reverse it as well?

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.040
Here are some answers.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.320
Legumes, by which they mean all kinds of

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.240
beans, chickpeas, split peas, and lentils,

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.160
are an excellent source of many essential

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.080
nutrients—vitamins, minerals, fibers,

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.960
antioxidants, and not
just an excellent source,

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.600
perhaps the single cheapest source.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:23.000
In terms of nutrition density per penny,

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.520
the four that really pull off

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:25.840
from the pack are pinto beans,

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:29.360
lentils, black beans, and kidney beans.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.880
And, all that nutritional quality

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.760
may have beneficial effects on

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.600
excess body weight, insulin resistance,

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:35.720
high cholesterol, inflammation,

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.840
and oxidative stress—

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.840
all major cardiovascular risk factors.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:42.040
So, do men and women who eat more

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:45.120
beans tend to have less heart disease?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.640
Yes, suggesting that increasing

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.840
legume intake may be an important part

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:51.160
of a dietary approach to the primary

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.880
prevention of coronary heart disease

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:53.960
in the general population,

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.200
meaning prevention of heart disease

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.080
in the first place.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.320
But, maybe those eating more

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.960
bean burritos are just eating

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.200
less beef burritos?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.720
They took that into account,

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.760
controlling for meat intake,

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.080
fruits, and vegetables
and smoking and exercise,

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.520
and still, the bean eaters

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.800
appeared to be protected.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.120
Note the highest category
here was eating

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.600
legumes 4 or more times a week.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.640
In my Daily Dozen, I recommend people

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.000
eat legumes three times—a day!

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.840
In Costa Rica, they were able to find

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.800
enough people eating beans every day,

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.720
and so, even after controlling for

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:30.640
many of the same things,

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.760
like intake of saturated
fat and cholesterol,

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.400
one bean serving a day was

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.440
associated with a 38% reduction

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.000
in the risk of heart attack.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.000
Yeah, but do you actually

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.440
get to live longer too?

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:47.320
Yes, apparently so, an 8%
lower all-cause mortality,

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:51.040
again after adjusting for
other dietary factors.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.640
You can’t control for everything, though.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:56.240
You can’t really prove cause
and effect until you…

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.240
put it to the test.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.080
Randomized controlled
interventional trials

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:02.400
have found that dietary bean intake

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.520
does significantly reduce

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.000
bad cholesterol levels,

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.720
dating back a half century to 1962.

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.440
Measure cholesterol levels at baseline,

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.600
and then add beans to their diet,

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.080
and then remove beans from their diet.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.320
And, look, beans have
a low glycemic index

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.640
and saturated fat content,

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.960
and are high in fiber,

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:25.120
potassium, and plant protein,

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.480
each of which independently confers

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:29.640
blood pressure-lowering effects.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.200
But, whether there’s sufficient evidence

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.880
to emphasize beans alone
to lower BP is unclear.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.760
Therefore, what we need is a

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.440
systematic review and meta-analysis

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.389
of controlled feeding trials and...

00:11:41.389 --> 00:11:43.200
here it is.
And, what they found is that beans

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.560
do indeed lower blood pressure

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.080
no matter where you start out.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.720
OK. So, beans may be able

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.040
to prevent artery disease,

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.200
but what about reversing it?

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:57.360
Can the daily consumption of beans—

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.520
other than soy,

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.360
reverse vascular impairment

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.640
due to peripheral artery disease?

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:04.320
Peripheral artery disease results

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.720
from a decrease in blood flow

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:07.680
to the legs due to a buildup

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.400
of atherosclerotic plaque higher up.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.960
Yeah, soybeans may help,

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.400
but what about other beans?

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.400
So, they had twenty-six individuals

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.160
with peripheral artery disease

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:21.360
consume one serving a day
of a combination of beans,

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.320
split peas, lentils, and
chickpeas for 8 weeks.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.800
Basically, how you diagnose
and follow-up the disease

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.040
is with the ankle-brachial index,

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.040
which is just the ratio of

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.320
blood pressure at your ankle

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:32.720
compared to your arm.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.600
Once it dips below point nine,

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:35.760
that means you must have some kind

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:39.240
of clogs in blood flow
to your lower body,

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.960
but eat some beans,

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.120
and you may get a significant increase,

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.440
enough to push four of 26 participants

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.240
up into the normal range

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.560
after just 8 weeks, eating some beans!

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.240
Now, there was no control group,

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:56.720
but people tend to get
worse, not better.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:57.720
The researchers conclude

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:00.720
a legume-rich diet can elicit major

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.173
improvements in arterial function.

